  goldReward: 500
  expReward: 100
  offerDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences:
    - "Now it's time to apply that concept."
    - "We need a bridge connecting the factory access road to the other side of the channel. Keep the lane <b><#E09500>closer to one side</color></b> to work around the existing equipment."
    - "We'll use an <b><#E09500>SUV</color></b> to test the crossing. Make sure the roadway and supports carry it safely from one bank to the other."
    - "In a real bridge, that off-center load can also create a <b><#E09500>twisting moment</color></b>. Keep the lesson in mind when considering the lane's position."
    - "Build around the conditions at this site, {PlayerName}. If you're ready, you can take the contract."
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences:
    - "Remember, we can't move the existing equipment to make room for your bridge."
    - "Keep the SUV's lane clear, check the roadway connections, and remember why an <b><#E09500>off-center load can create torsion</color></b> in a real bridge."
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences:
    - "Good work, {PlayerName}. The crossing fits the site, and the factory can keep operating without us moving the existing equipment."
    - "You worked with the conditions instead of expecting the site to accommodate your design."
    - "You've also considered why the <b><#E09500>position of a load matters when torsion comes into play</color></b>."
    - "There's a larger equipment project ahead. After we review this lesson, <b><#E09500>Mills</color></b> is the person to speak to about it."
